   - Multiply the mass per milliliter by the desired volume (10 mL):  
     \[
     10 \text{ mL} \times 0.000044 \text{ mg/mL} = 0.44 \text{ mg}
     \]

Thus, there is $\boxed{0.44 \text{ mg}}$ of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose.
