","To calculate the standard enthalpy change for the reaction, we use the enthalpy of formation of the product and the enthalpies of hydration of the reactants. The reaction is:

\[
\text{Fe}^{}^{2+} + 6 \text{H}_2\text{O} + 2 \text{Cl}^-] \rightarrow \text{FeCl}_4^2- + 6 \text{H}_2\text{O}
\]

The standard enthalpy change (\(\Delta H_f^f\)) for the reaction can be calculated using the following equation:

\[
\Delta H = \Delta H_f^f(\text{product}) - \Delta H_F_{\text{reactants}}
\]

In this case, the product is \(\text{FeCl}_4(2-]\) and the reactants are \(\text{Fe}^{}^{2+}\) and \(\text{Cl}^-\). The enthalpy of formation for \(\text{FeCl}_4(2^{-}\) is given as \(-392 \, \text{kJ/mol}\). The enthalpies of hydration are given for \(\text{Fe}^{}^{2+}\) and \(\text{Cl}^-\).

The enthalpy of formation for a complex is calculated as:
\[
\Delta H_f = \Delta H_f(\text{ complex ion}) - \sum \Delta H_{\text{hydation of ions in complex ion}}
\]
Thus, the enthalpy of formation for \(\text{Fe}^{}^{2+}\) with \(6\text{H}_2\text{O}\) is \(\Delta H_f = \Delta H_{\text{hydation of } \text{Fe}^{}^{2+}} = -340 \, \text{kJ/mol}\).
The enthalpy of formation for \(\text{Cl}^-\) with \(H__2\text{O}\) is \(\Delta H_f = \Delta H_{\text{hydation of } \text{Cl}^-} = -381 \, \text{kJ/mol}}\).

The enthalpy change for the reaction is:
\[
\Delta H = \Delta H_f^{\text{hydlysis of } \text{Fe}^{}^{2+}} + 2\Delta H_{\text{hydation of } \text{Cl}^-} - \Delta H_f^{\text{hydylation of } \text{FeCl}_4}^2^-
\]
