2. **Counting Chloride Ions:**  
   - The formula \([ \text{PCl}_{4} \text{Cl}_2 \text{Cl}_2 \) indicates two chloride ions (\(\text{Cl}^-\)) bound directly to the complex ion.  
   - The formula also indicates two additional chloride ions (\(\text{Cl}^^-}\)) as separate chloride ions.  
3. **Total:**  
   - Total chloride ions = 2 (from the complex) + 2 (as separate ions) = 4  

