\[
\Delta H = (-340 \, \text{kJ/mol} + 2(-381 \, \text{kJ/mol}) - (-392 \, \text{kJ/mol}) = -340 - 762 + 392 = -710 \, \text{kJ/mol}
\]

Thus, the standard enthalpy change for the reaction is \(-710 \, \text{kJ/mol}\).

