","The symmetric difference of two sets \( A \) and \( B \) is given by \( A \triangle b = (A \setminus B) \cup (B \setminus A) = (A \circ B) \setminus (A \cap B) \).
The given statement is that \( A \triangle B \leq A \), which means that all elements in \( A \triangle B \) are also in \( A \).
Thus, \( A \triangle B = ((A \ominus B) \circ (B \ominus A)) \leq A \).
