The hydrolysis of ATP is the reverse of the formation of ATP from ADP and Pi:
\[
\text{ADP} + \text{P}_i \rightarrow \text{ATP} + \text{H}_2\text{O} \quad \text{(ATP formation)}
\]
The standard free energy change for this reaction is \(\boxed{-30.5 \text{ kJ/mol}}\).
Since the reaction is not spontaneous (positive \Delta G), the hydrolysis of ATP is required to drive it forward.

